LIO['reg2']={'title': 'Book and AUM regressions agree: ~255-310p on the peer lines', 'img1': 'lio_pbroe.png', 'img2': 'lio_evaum2.png', 'note': 'PBR: ROE = 14.5 x P/B - 5.1 (R² 0.94); log fit ROE = 23.0 ln(P/B) + 11.4 (R² 0.73); n=11. EV/AUM: EV/AUM(%) = 0.0506 x E/AUM(bp) + 0.0097 (R² 0.69); n=10 ex-Ashmore. Forward ROE = FY+1 consensus EPS x shares / latest book equity; E = FY+1 consensus EBIT; AUM latest reported (Aberdeen AUMA incl. platform; USD at 1.311).', 'read': ['**PBR vs ROE:** at a ~20% forward ROE the linear line implies 1.73x P/B (log 1.45x) vs 1.29x actual, ~255-300p per share', '**EV/AUM vs E/AUM:** ~12bp of FY+1 EBIT on AUM implies 0.61% EV/AUM vs 0.40% actual; EV ~£148m plus net cash, ~300-310p', 'The EV/AUM slope (0.0506) means the sector pays ~5x EBIT for AUM earnings - the multiple used in our SOTP', 'Caveat: book equity is 87% goodwill/intangibles, so P/B flatters; the R² of 0.94 is driven partly by Polar Capital']}
